Third-party components
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Orbweaver's licensing policy is: MIT for everything we write; where a component
is *data we cannot originate* — a character mapping table, a timezone database
— a permissive-with-attribution licence is accepted, disclosed here, and
recorded as a decision under docs/decisions/.

The distinction is deliberate. Logic defined by a published specification we
implement ourselves and owe nobody anything for; that is why the ORB core is
first-party work. A mapping table is somebody's compilation of facts, with no
specification to implement it from, and retyping it produces the same derived
work rather than an original one.

